sequenceDiagram
    participant DSWorkload as Data Science Workloads
    participant Prometheus as Prometheus<br/>9090/TCP<br/>TLS (service-ca)
    participant ClusterProxy as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>(cluster-proxy)<br/>8443/TCP TLS
    participant NSProxy as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>(namespace-proxy)<br/>8443/TCP TLS
    participant PromLabel as prom-label-proxy<br/>9090/TCP
    participant Route as OpenShift Routes<br/>HTTPS/TLS
    participant Client as External Client
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP TLS 1.2+
    participant Webhook as Webhook Server<br/>9443/TCP TLS
    participant Reconciler as MonitoringReconciler
    participant Collector as OTel Collector<br/>8889/TCP
    participant Loki as LokiStack

    Note over DSWorkload, Prometheus: Flow 1: Metrics Collection and Proxy Access

    DSWorkload->>Prometheus: Metrics scrape<br/>9090/TCP HTTP<br/>TLS (service-ca) / ServiceAccount
    Client->>Route: GET /metrics<br/>HTTPS/TLS
    Route->>ClusterProxy: Forward request<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS
    ClusterProxy->>K8sAPI: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview<br/>metrics.k8s.io/nodes/get
    K8sAPI-->>ClusterProxy: Auth result
    ClusterProxy->>Prometheus: Proxy to upstream<br/>9090/TCP HTTPS<br/>mTLS (client cert + CA)
    Prometheus-->>ClusterProxy: Metrics response
    ClusterProxy-->>Route: Response
    Route-->>Client: Metrics data

    Note over K8sAPI, Webhook: Flow 2: Admission Webhook Injection

    K8sAPI->>Webhook: Admission Request<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS<br/>TLS (cert-manager)
    Note right of Webhook: PodMonitor/ServiceMonitor<br/>CREATE or UPDATE
    Webhook->>Webhook: Read namespace labels<br/>Determine injection targets
    Webhook->>K8sAPI: Mutated response<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS/WSS<br/>TLS 1.2+ / ServiceAccount
    K8sAPI-->>Webhook: Acknowledgment

    Note over Reconciler, K8sAPI: Flow 3: Controller Reconciliation

    Reconciler->>K8sAPI: Watch Monitoring CR<br/>+ dependent resources<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS/WSS<br/>TLS 1.2+ / ServiceAccount
    K8sAPI-->>Reconciler: Change event
    Reconciler->>Reconciler: Render Go templates<br/>into K8s manifests
    Reconciler->>K8sAPI: Server-Side Apply<br/>(Deployments, Secrets,<br/>ConfigMaps, Services,<br/>Routes, RBAC, NetworkPolicies)

    Note over Collector, Loki: Flow 4: Usage Log Collection

    DSWorkload->>Collector: Metrics/logs<br/>8889/TCP
    Collector->>Loki: Forward usage logs<br/>to LokiStack
